WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.037
-The president mounted
an appallingly racist attack

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.105
on four Democratic women
of color in Congress.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.441
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:12.278
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.914
It's been obvious from
the very first moment he stepped

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.883
onto the political stage
that Donald Trump is a racist,

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:21.187
and that racism is at the core
of his political ideology.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.656
It's not a side dish.
It's the main course.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.993
Every day, he serves up
a steaming hot entree of racism

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.462
and then washes it down
with a side of...

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.898
-McDonald's, Wendy's,
and Burger King for some pizza.

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:34.567
[ Laughter, cheers ]

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.368
-Trump launched
his political career

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:39.071
by questioning legitimacy
of the first black president,

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:40.673
began his campaign by claiming

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.175
Mexico is sending criminals
and rapists to the U.S.,

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:44.877
and said a judge who
was overseeing a lawsuit

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.145
against him in 2016

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.913
shouldn't be allowed
to oversee the case

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:49.816
because of his ethnicity.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:52.284
-Now, this judge
is of Mexican heritage.

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.654
I'm building a wall, okay?
I'm building a wall.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.723
-But you're invoking his race
when talking about

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:57.991
whether or not
he can do his job.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.059
-Jake, I'm building a wall.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:01.627
Okay?
I'm building a wall.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:06.098
-If you are saying he can't
do his job because of his race,

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:08.634
is that not
the definition of racism?

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.336
-No, I don't think so at all.
-No?

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:13.205
-No. He's proud of his heritage.
I respect him for that.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:14.808
-You're saying he can't do
his job because of that.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.742
-Look, he's proud
of his heritage, okay?

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:18.210
I'm building a wall.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.579
This judge is giving us
unfair rulings.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:22.114
Now I say, why?

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:23.816
Well, I'm building a wall.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:27.620
-Okay, but why won't you
tell us what you're building?

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.888
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.023
He keeps saying it over and over
like he's wearing a wire

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:32.192
and calling for backup.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.560
"I'm building a wall.
I'm building a wall.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.230
Wall!
Steve, get me out of here!"

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.831
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:41.100
So, Trump launched
a racist attack on a judge

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.068
by calling him unqualified
to rule in a case

00:01:43.068 --> 00:01:44.871
because of their ethnicity,
and, by the way,

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.472
in case you're somehow
still curious about

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:47.973
Donald Trump's legal bona fides,

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.409
here's what he had
to say on Friday about

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.011
Special Counsel Robert Mueller's
report which listed

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.847
10 possible instances
of obstruction of justice.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.316
Remember, 10. 10!

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.750
Somehow, everyone's
forgotten about that,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.518
because it was like
50 scandals ago.

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:01.187
We all have such scandal
fatigue,

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.789
at this point,
Trump could streak naked

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.923
across the White House lawn

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.390
with his head stuck
in a KFC bucket,

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.559
screaming, "I did it.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:09.061
I broke all the laws,"
and two days later,

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.229
we'll all be scratching
our heads, going,

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.765
"Oh, yeah, right.
That happened."

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:15.134
So, Trump was asked about
the Mueller report on Friday,

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.436
and he tried to claim that
Article 2 of the Constitution

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:19.605
gives him the power to,
basically, do whatever he wants.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:21.540
Now, remember,
this is the same guy

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.243
who said a judge wasn't
qualified to rule on a case

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:26.078
because of
that judge's ethnicity.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:28.180
By comparison,
here's Trump talking about

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.317
Article 2 of the Constitution
of the United States.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.485
-Number one, there's no crime.

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:36.355
And how do you obstruct
when there's no crime?

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.658
Also, take a look
at one other thing.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.126
It's a thing called Article 2.

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:43.362
Nobody ever mentions Article 2.

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:46.165
It gives me all of these rights

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.467
at a level that nobody
has ever seen before.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.602
We don't even talk
about Article 2.

00:02:50.602 --> 00:02:53.973
-what do you mean,
nobody has ever seen before?

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.242
It was written
over 200 years ago.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:59.312
just because you've
never seen it before

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.781
doesn't mean
nobody's ever seen it before.

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.383
"I just saw this great
little independent film.

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:07.153
No one's ever seen it before,
called 'The Lion King.'"

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.153
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.156
it's about a good
guy named Scar,

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.957
but oh, he's got
a real a [bleep] nephew

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:14.060
who tries to backstab him.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.728
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.896
But I like Scar --

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.364
I haven't finished it.
It's two hours long.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.999
That's too long.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.702
But I like Scar's chances.
I think --

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:26.872
I think it's gonna end well
for Scar."

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:29.842
Also his interpretation of
Article 2 is obviously wrong,

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.077
which is not surprising

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.745
since he, apparently,
just discovered it.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.113
"Here's another thing
I just learned.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:37.183
Did you know we had a president
who was 100 feet tall?

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.785
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:43.389
Made of stone."

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.590
What we saw in that interview

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.559
was the core of Trump's
racist world view,

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.160
and we saw yet again on Sunday

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.363
when Trump launched
a stunningly racist attack

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.398
On four progressive women
of color in Congress.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.901
-The President
of the United States

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:58.237
told progressive Democratic
women of color in Congress

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:02.774
to go back to the crime-infested
places from which they came.

00:04:02.774 --> 00:04:04.776
Trump writing this --

00:04:04.776 --> 00:04:06.445
"So interesting to see

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:08.614
progressive
Democrat Congresswomen

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:10.583
who originally
came from countries

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.519
Whose governments are a complete
and total catastrophe,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:16.989
The worst, most corrupt,
and inept anywhere in the world,

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:20.192
If they even have
a functioning government at all,

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:21.960
now loudly and viciously

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.963
telling the people
of the United States,

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.599
the greatest and most powerful
nation on Earth,

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:29.201
how our government is to be run.

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:31.670
Why don't they go back
and help fix

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.439
the totally broken
and crime-infested places

00:04:34.439 --> 00:04:36.175
from which they came?

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:39.411
Then come back
and show us how it is done.

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:41.948
These places
need your help badly.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.816
You can't leave fast enough.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.351
I'm sure that Nancy Pelosi

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.519
would be very happy
to quickly work out

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:50.022
free travel arrangements."

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:52.592
-Okay, first of all,
there's no acceptable word

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.527
for this other than racist,
period.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.995
Not racially charged
or racially tinged or,

00:04:56.995 --> 00:04:58.230
as "The New York Times" put it,

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.266
Trump's racially-
infused politics,

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.034
like it's some kind
of fancy drink

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:04.136
At a Williamsburg cocktail bar.

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:08.907
"Oh, honey, their cosmo
is racially infused."

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:11.844
Second,
this is beside the point,

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.780
but three of the Congresswomen
you're attacking were born here,

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.449
and they're all
American citizens.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.584
So, if you're asking them to fix

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.620
the totally broken
crime-infested governments

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:24.456
of their home countries,
they're trying.

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:27.426
[ Laughter, cheering ]

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.428
It doesn't matter...

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.929
Doesn't matter whether

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:32.832
they were born here or not,
they're Americans.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.734
This is their country,
and they are treating it

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.402
with a lot more
respect and devotion

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.270
than the racist gargoyle
who sits around,

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.539
tweeting from the back nine
of his chintzy golf course.

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:41.741
I mean, look at that.

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:43.109
That looks like a sculpture

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:47.113
someone would build
to make fun of Donald Trump.

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:51.784
I call this one
"The Melting Racist."

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.285
And then today
Trump reeled off

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:55.822
yet another racist tirade
at a White House event called

00:05:55.822 --> 00:05:57.723
the "Made in America"
product showcase.

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.291
First, he took questions
from reporters

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:02.295
and defended his tweet
when asked if they were racist.

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:03.663
-Not at all.

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:05.664
-Democratic Congresswomen
are not American?

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:08.234
-Somebody has a problem
with our country,

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:09.902
if somebody doesn't want
to be in our country,

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:10.736
they should leave.

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:11.771
-I think it's very fitting

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.005
that he's standing
next to a boat

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.473
because he always looks
like he just fell off

00:06:14.473 --> 00:06:15.707
the side of a booze cruise

00:06:15.707 --> 00:06:18.777
and got dragged back onto deck
by a lifeguard.

00:06:18.777 --> 00:06:20.479
Then Trump moved
over to the podium

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:21.748
where he continued his tirade

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:23.582
and doubled down
on those racist tweets.

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:26.285
-If you're not happy
in the U.S.,

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:28.621
if you're complaining
all the time,

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.422
very simply, you can leave.

00:06:30.422 --> 00:06:32.324
You can leave right now.

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:34.426
Come back if you want.
Don't come back.

00:06:34.426 --> 00:06:35.761
It's okay, too.

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:38.197
But if you're not happy,
you can leave.

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:40.533
-I'm sorry, you're accusing
someone else of comp--

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:42.468
All you do is complain.

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.971
You spent the eight years
of Obama's presidency

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.572
lying and complaining
about everything.

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:48.206
In fact, at one point,
you actually bragged

00:06:48.206 --> 00:06:50.709
about the fact that
you were great at whining.

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:52.578
-I am the most fabulous whiner.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:55.081
I do whine because
I want to win.

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:57.349
And I'm not hap--
-Are whiners winners?

00:06:57.349 --> 00:06:59.552
-And I am a whiner,
and I'm a whiner,

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:02.221
and I keep whining and whining
until I win.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:06.225
-That is a terrible
Dr. Seuss book.

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:08.994
"I keep whining and whining
until I'm a winner.

00:07:08.994 --> 00:07:11.998
And then I go home
and have pizza for dinner."

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:14.634
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.937
Trump's attack on four
progressive women of color

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:20.806
wasn't just blatantly
and appallingly racist,

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:22.408
it's also a classic
racist trope.

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:24.576
It's the kind of taunt
and insult people of color

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:26.178
have been
subjected to for years,

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:27.980
as Senator Kamala Harris
explained.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.482
-It's absolutely racist
and un-American,

00:07:30.482 --> 00:07:32.284
and it is an old trope --

00:07:32.284 --> 00:07:34.820
"Go back to where
you came from."

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:38.524
You might hear it on the street,
but should never hear that

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:40.426
from the President
of the United States.

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.993
-And she's right.
Trump shouldn't be president.

00:07:41.993 --> 00:07:43.262
At best, he should
be on the street

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.831
selling fake Rolexes
in Times Square

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:48.166
and yelling at tourists
for not buying them.

00:07:48.166 --> 00:07:51.370
"Oh, what?!
You never heard of a Polex?"

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.338
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:54.774
What we're seeing now,
once again,

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:58.176
is the core of Trump's racist
ideology and policy agenda.

00:07:58.176 --> 00:08:00.545
His administration is
inflicting cruelty on migrants

00:08:00.545 --> 00:08:02.248
through inhumane
detention centers,

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:03.549
family separation,

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:05.952
and he spent his career
questioning the legitimacy

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:07.719
of everyone
from the first black president

00:08:07.719 --> 00:08:09.455
to judges
to members of Congress.

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:11.023
What more do you need
to impeach this guy?

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:12.859
Congress should
just say to him...

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:15.027
-You can leave.
You can leave right now.

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.529
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:18.030
[ Cheers and applause ]

